<section id="poem" class="card-poem">
    <div
        class="flex flex-col md:flex-row justify-center items-center gap-8 md:gap-12 p-6 md:p-8"
    >
        <div class="text-base flex flex-col items-center text-center max-w-sm">
            <h1 class="poem-title">
                'Hope' is the thing with feathers
            </h1>
            <p class="text-slate-300 mt-1">
                ~ <a
                    href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emily_Dickinson"
                    class="underline decoration-dotted text-slate-300"
                    >Emily Dickinson</a
                >
            </p>
            <img
                src="/assets/bird.jpg"
                alt="Emily Dickinson's poem illustration"
                class="avatar-circular mt-6"
            />

            <a
                href="https://youtu.be/g5wEqF7NtcI?list=PLE2EF7yo6iH3O8a3QkUn9F8bQEYOb51sg"
                target="_blank"
                rel="noopener noreferrer"
                class="w-full block mt-5"
            >
                <button
                    class="btn-secondary"
                >
                    Recitation by Mairin O'Hagan
                </button>
            </a>
        </div>

        <p
            class="poem-lyrics"
        >
            'Hope' is the thing with feathers -<br />
            That perches in the soul -<br />
            And sings the tune without the words -<br />
            And never stops - at all - <br />
            <br />
            And sweetest - in the Gale - is heard -<br />
            And sore must be the storm -<br />
            That could abash the little Bird<br />
            That kept so many warm -<br /><br />
            I’ve heard it in the chillest land -<br />
            And on the strangest Sea -<br />
            Yet - never - in Extremity,<br />
            It asked a crumb - of me.<br />
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
